course: dictionary
lesson: 15497
title: Stunned: surprised or hit
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Stunned has two main meanings. The first is very surprised or shocked, so that you can hardly speak or move. The second is made dizzy or unconscious for a short time by a hit on the head.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to use. «The crowd was stunned into silence after the final goal.» Nobody was hurt, and people went quiet, so stunned means shocked and amazed.
explain: «The ball hit Sam on the head, and he was stunned for a moment.» A hit and a moment on the ground are the clues. Here stunned means dizzy for a short time. Try your meaning in the sentence: does "Sam was shocked for a moment" make sense after a ball hits his head? It does not, so the meaning is dizzy.
fact: Stunned is the past form of the verb stun. Stun, stuns, stunned and stunning all belong to one family.
fact: «Stunned» means very surprised or shocked, so that you can hardly speak or move.
fact: «Stunned» can also mean made unconscious or dizzy for a short time by a hit on the head.
fact: Learn these phrases: «stunned silence», «stunned into silence», and «stunned by the news».
fact: Check the clues: surprise makes people go quiet, while a hit makes people dizzy.
exercise: «Mia was stunned into silence when she opened her present.» What does stunned mean here? | Made dizzy by a hit on the head | Hungry after a long day | *Very surprised, so she could hardly speak | Cold and wet from the rain
exercise: «The ball hit Sam on the head, and he was stunned for a moment.» What does stunned mean here? | Very surprised by a gift | *Dizzy or unconscious for a short time after a hit | Happy and laughing | Tired after a long run
exercise: «The bird flew into the window and lay stunned on the grass.» What happened to the bird? | It was given a present | It flew away happily | It was very hungry | *It was made dizzy for a short time
test: «The news was so big that the whole room was stunned.» What does stunned mean? | Cold and wet | Angry at the teacher | *Very shocked, so no one could speak | Very sleepy
test: Which phrase from the lesson means quiet because someone is very surprised? | *Stunned silence | Noisy party | Wet grass | Fast run
exam: «The ball stunned the goalkeeper for a second.» What does stunned mean here? | Very surprised by the score | *Made dizzy or unconscious for a short time by a hit | Calm and relaxed | Very hungry after the match
